{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>[The woman] whom you placed with me:</b> You gave the one who gave to me. And the sense of עמדי is \"with me, in the garden,\" and it is like עמי. But we do not find it except in the language of a singular speaker." "וָאֹכל — the alef is a sign of the first person, and the hidden [letter] that comes after it is in place of the root alef, and it comes with kamatz katan because it is the end of a verse. And it is not possible for a vav with kamatz to come with the verb, for it is always with shva."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:59.059377359Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}